{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If you walk in My statutes</b> — in gematria: עמלים in words of Torah. It juxtaposed 'if in My statutes' to 'Sabbath' to say that they are equivalent to all the commandments and statutes. And further, it juxtaposed Sabbath to 'I will give your rains in their season' — that is, on Sabbath nights." "<b>If you walk in My statutes</b> — ראשי תיבות: אבות, that you walk in the path of the fathers. 'In My statutes you walk' — this is fear, as written 'The fear of YHWH, it is His treasure' — if you fill His treasuries, I will fill your treasuries: 'May YHWH open for you His treasure.'" "<b>And you shall do them</b> — letters of אמת. Or: that you engage in Torah, for 'making' is written of it, 'every good to those who do them.' Ten verses from 'If in My statutes' (i.e., from 'I will give') until 'and I will lead you upright' — corresponding to the ten blessings therein given to you, and corresponding to the Ten Commandments."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:42.328203407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}